        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/10",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Non-tender (2) Service time, projected arbitration salaries (public estimates exist) and the non-tender list are public, but the replacement pool is revealed only after the deadline. A forecast of who will be available must be made without hindsight, and that is the hard part.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/11",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Non-tender (3) Roughly two decades of non-tender classes exist, but the CBA has changed salary and service rules, so older cases may not be comparable. Next-season output of non-tendered players is observable, but the output of the counterfactual tendered player is not, and survivorship in who signs where biases the comparison.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/12",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Non-tender (4,5) It is actionable, since the club decides by the deadline. Clubs already use WAR-per-dollar thresholds, and public arbitration projection tools exist, so the marginal edge is likely small.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/13",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Non-tender (6) A backtest looks good when it credits signed non-tendered players' production without netting out the many who flopped or were never signed, or when it uses the final arbitration salary instead of the projection known in November.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/14",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Qualifying offers (1) The Cubs face the decision only for their own eligible free agents, which may be zero to a few per year. The stake is a one-year QO salary against a draft-pick change, so the value is moderate and lumpy. UNKNOWN: cubs_qo_eligible_players_2026",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/15",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Qualifying offers (2) Performance, age and the QO amount are public. Acceptance depends on private player preferences and agent strategy.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/16",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Qualifying offers (3) The number of historical QOs is a few dozen per year at most, with an early period of nearly zero acceptances and a later period with some, so the pooled model is small and non-stationary. Acceptance is observable, but the counterfactual of not offering is not. UNKNOWN: historical_qo_acceptance_count_by_year",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/17",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Qualifying offers (4,5) It is actionable in a short window after the World Series. Clubs reason about this with simple market-versus-QO logic, and a sharper model probably adds little over an experienced executive.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/18",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Qualifying offers (6) A high AUC in-sample may come from a few features (large AAV expectation means decline) that the baseline already uses. Rule changes to compensation across CBAs also confound the pooled history.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/19",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "NPB/KBO posting bids (1) Few relevant events per year, so recurrence is low, but the per-signing value can be large. Cubs interest in a given year is unknown. UNKNOWN: cubs_international_budget_2027",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/20",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "NPB/KBO (2) Basic stats are public, but detailed pitch tracking is mostly proprietary or inconsistently published, so the translation tool may only have stats the baseline ratios already use. UNKNOWN: public_availability_of_npb_kbo_pitch_tracking",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/21",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "NPB/KBO (3) The number of posted players with several MLB seasons is small, probably tens, split across hitters and pitchers and across ball and rule eras. A model with many parameters will overfit. Outcomes are observable but heterogeneous by role and injury. UNKNOWN: count_of_posted_players_with_mlb_outcomes",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/22",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "NPB/KBO (4,5) Bids are actionable only in a short, rule-bound window and posting fees and caps depend on current agreements. Clubs with international scouts and data staff already model translation, and the price is set by multi-club competition, so the winner's curse may erase any accuracy edge.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/23",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "NPB/KBO (6) It looks useful through survivorship (only successes recalled), a few outlier stars driving fit, and comparing to the weakest ratio baseline instead of scouting-informed pricing.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/24",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Postseason roster construction (1) It recurs only when the club qualifies, 1 to 4 times a year, so expected value is discounted by playoff probability. A marginal win may be worth more in October, but the number of slots that actually change outcomes is small. UNKNOWN: measured_win_probability_value_of_marginal_postseason_slot",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/25",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Postseason (2) Rosters, platoon and pitch-type splits are public, but injury status at the roster deadline is often incomplete or vague, which limits reconstruction of the true option set. UNKNOWN: public_injury_status_completeness_at_roster_deadline",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/26",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Postseason (3) Postseason rosters from many series exist league-wide, but the per-series sample is tiny and series outcomes are very noisy. A test would need to score recommendations by simulated expected win probability, and the simulation embeds the same assumptions it tests, so it is not an observed-outcome validation.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/27",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Postseason (4,5) It is actionable and contenders already do this internally with staff judgment, so a public tool likely only matches.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/28",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Postseason (6) It looks useful through hindsight-chosen anecdotes (a pinch runner who scored), unmeasurable gains of well under a percentage point of series win probability, and ignoring that managers concentrate innings on top pitchers whatever the 26th slot is. Note the candidate text supplied for this item lists only the decision, and the problem is narrower than its attached assumptions suggest.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/29",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Arbitration filing (1) The Cubs file for each arbitration-eligible player every winter, which is several per year, with award differences per player in the range between filing numbers. Most cases settle, and hearings are rare for any one club.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/30",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Arbitration (2) Hearing outcomes and filing figures are publicly reported, but the panel's reasoning is confidential, and settlement terms are inconsistently recorded. Comparable-player selection rules are set by the CBA, which may change after this offseason. UNKNOWN: post_2026_cba_arbitration_rules",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/31",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Arbitration (3) League-wide hearings are only a handful per year, so a predictor trained on hearings suffers from small samples and a selection effect: cases that reach hearing are those where the parties disagree, not a random draw. Outcome (win or loss against the two filed numbers) is observable. UNKNOWN: annual_hearing_count_sample_size",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/32",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Arbitration (4,5) Actionable by choosing the filing figure and deciding whether to settle. Clubs already employ specialized staff and outside counsel, and public salary-projection tools exist. A club-policy of avoiding hearings (a \"file and trial\" posture) also carries relationship costs a model does not capture.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/33",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Arbitration (6) It looks useful through high accuracy that merely reflects the filing midpoint, hindsight about which stats panels reward, and treating the all-case outcome rate as if it applied to the cases a club would actually take to hearing.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/34",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "BLIND SPOT (a) All six are low-frequency, small-sample decisions. The set concentrates on offseason transactions and leaves out high-frequency decisions with larger samples, which the objective preferred.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/35",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "BLIND SPOT (b) Five of six depend on CBA rules that may change this offseason. The expiration timing is unverified. UNKNOWN: cba_expiration_date_verification",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/36",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "BLIND SPOT (c) Every candidate's retrospective test measures outcomes of decisions made, not outcomes of the unchosen option. Counterfactuals are unobserved, and models validated on simulation inherit simulation bias.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/37",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "BLIND SPOT (d) No candidate states a baseline hit rate or dollar scale from supplied evidence, so the value-at-stake comparison is unsupported. UNKNOWN: cubs_private_models_and_practices",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/38",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "BLIND SPOT (e) Software cost, adoption by decision-makers and the chance that clubs already run equivalent tools are not weighed against the possible edge. A null result is itself informative and cheap to get, so testing before building is the reasonable default.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1/claim/39",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Sharpened replacement: one pooled \"decision-quality audit\" that, for non-tender, QO and arbitration decisions, uses only timestamped public data (projections and prices known on decision day) and reports the gap versus the simple baseline with bootstrap intervals. Build more only for the decision where the interval excludes zero by a margin larger than the dollar noise, and report a null for the others.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        }
      ],
