        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/10",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Coaching 3] The number of coach-movement events with enough players per coach is probably small, and the outcome (player change) is observable but very noisy. Intervals may be too wide to change any hiring decision.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/11",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Coaching 4] Actionability is limited because the Cubs can hire only from available candidates, and coach quality is hard to separate from the hiring club's infrastructure.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/12",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Coaching 5] Sophisticated clubs probably already track player development outcomes by staff internally. Public sources give mostly anecdote and press narrative, not rigorous attribution.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/13",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Coaching 6] It would look useful through regression to the mean, survivorship (coaches get poached after good years), and teams acquiring players they already expect to improve. Pitch-mix changes may be driven by front-office strategy and not by the coach.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/14",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "persistence_of_coach_effects_year_over_year",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/15",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Non-tender 1] The decision recurs every November or December, but the Cubs' marginal cases (borderline tender candidates) are probably few per year. Stake per case is the gap between arbitration salary and replacement cost.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/16",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Non-tender 2] Public arbitration salary projections and the prior-year non-tender lists are public. The set of players other clubs will non-tender is not known when the Cubs decide, so any replacement-pool label built from the final list leaks hindsight unless it is forecast as of a dated snapshot.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/17",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Non-tender 3] Past decisions are many league-wide, and signing price and next-season output are observable. Players signed after non-tender are a selected sample, because injured or declining players are overrepresented.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/18",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Non-tender 4] Actionability is high and cheap to reverse. A club can tender, then trade or release, with partial cost, which weakens the need for a precise model.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/19",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Non-tender 5] Clubs already apply WAR-per-dollar thresholds with internal projections, and public arbitration projections are widely available.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/20",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Non-tender 6] It would look useful through hindsight-labeled replacement pools, and through backtests that count only the non-tendered players who succeeded. A comparison against a strawman threshold also flatters it.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/21",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "historical_nontender_signing_outcomes_dataset",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/22",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[QO 1] The decision recurs yearly only for players who are QO-eligible, so per-year count may be zero to a few. Stake is a compensation pick versus a one-year salary, and the pick's value depends on CBA terms I could not verify.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/23",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "cubs_qo_eligible_players_2026",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/24",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "current_qo_amount_2026",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/25",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[QO 2] Public data on age, WAR, and market depth is available at decision time. Agent intent and private willingness to accept are not public, and they dominate the acceptance outcome.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/26",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[QO 3] Public history since the system began is only on the order of a hundred or so offers in total. That is too small for a calibrated model with many features, and each outcome is binary, which makes calibration weak.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/27",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "historical_qo_acceptance_count_by_year",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/28",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[QO 4] The CBA expires around December 2026 (unverified), so QO rules may change right when the model would be used, and backtests may not transfer.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/29",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "cba_expiration_date_verification",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/30",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[QO 5] Clubs and public analysts already compare projected market AAV to the QO amount, so the mechanism is largely the baseline stated in the IDEA.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/31",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[QO 6] It would look useful by overfitting a few dozen cases and by crediting hindsight on acceptance outcomes that were driven by market shocks.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/32",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Posting 1] Posting events per year are few, and the Cubs bid on a small fraction. Stake per signing is large, but the recurrence is thin.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/33",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "count_of_posted_players_with_mlb_outcomes",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/34",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Posting 2] Public NPB and KBO stats exist, but pitch-tracking and bat-tracking granularity may not be public or licensed. Whether posting timing and the player's availability are known at decision time varies by year.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/35",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "public_availability_of_npb_kbo_pitch_tracking",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/36",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Posting 3] The retrospective sample is small and heterogeneous across pitchers and hitters, ages, and ball and rule eras. MLB outcomes are observable but strongly censored by injury and playing time.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/37",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Posting 4] Actionability depends on posting fees, bid rules, and competition from other clubs. Any accuracy edge must also beat the winner's curse.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/38",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Posting 5] Clubs with international scouting and data feeds already run translation models. Public analysts publish translation factors, so the baseline \"simple ratios\" is probably weaker than actual club practice.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/39",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Posting 6] It would look useful through a handful of memorable hits and misses, and through fitting a model on survivors who were posted because they looked good. Narrow intervals from few cases would be false precision.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/40",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Postseason 1] The decision occurs only when the Cubs qualify, so expected annual value is discounted by playoff probability, and the number of roster slots that matter is small.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/41",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "measured_win_probability_value_of_marginal_postseason_slot",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/42",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Postseason 2] Opponent and roster information is public only close to the decision time. Injury status at the roster deadline is often incomplete.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/43",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "public_injury_status_completeness_at_roster_deadline",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/44",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Postseason 3] Public postseason series number only in the dozens each year, and outcomes are dominated by luck. A series win-probability difference of a fraction of a percentage point cannot be detected.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/45",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Postseason 4] Actionable, but constrained by health and by who is actually on the 40-man roster, which leaves few real choices.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/46",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Postseason 5] Contending clubs likely simulate matchups internally and have far better injury information than public sources.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/47",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Postseason 6] It would look useful by scoring simulator-recommended rosters against actual rosters on the same simulator, which only validates the model against itself. Post-hoc stories about a pinch runner are also misleading.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/48",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Arbitration 1] The decision recurs each January for every arbitration-eligible player, so many decisions per year, though hearings are a small subset. The stake is raise levels that compound, and the total is plausibly meaningful but unsized here.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/49",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "annual_hearing_count_sample_size",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/50",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Arbitration 2] Exchanged figures and hearing results are public. Panel reasoning, comparables admitted and club-specific hearing policy are less visible, and rules may change under a new CBA.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/51",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "post_2026_cba_arbitration_rules",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/52",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Arbitration 3] Hearings per year are few, so a panel-outcome predictor trained on public hearings has small n, and the outcome is binary (the panel picks one of two numbers), which carries little information per case.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/53",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Arbitration 4] Actionability is real for the file-and-trial and settlement choice, but a club policy choice (such as whether to go to hearings at all) can matter more than case-by-case prediction.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/54",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Arbitration 5] Clubs and outside counsel have studied hearings for decades, and settlement at midpoint is a well-known baseline. Public databases of arbitration results already exist.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/55",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Arbitration 6] It would look useful by fitting hearing results with too many features, and from selection: hearings are cases the sides could not settle, so they differ from the cases the model would need to price.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/56",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 1] No candidate states expected dollars or wins per decision with a source, so ranking by size of stake is currently unsupported.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/57",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 2] Every backtest compares against a simple rule, whereas the real competitor is internal staff with private data. Beating the strawman does not show an advantage.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/58",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 3] Hindsight risk is shared by all six. Backtests need dated snapshots of what was public at the decision date (projections, rosters, rumors), and many public sources are overwritten.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/59",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 4] Small n and multiple testing across features, years and subgroups will produce spurious wins for the QO, posting, postseason, and hearing candidates unless the test is pre-registered.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/60",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 5] A CBA expiration around this offseason (unverified) could change arbitration, QO, draft and service rules, and could cause a lockout. Backtests before that date may not carry over.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/61",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 6] Winner's curse and counterparty behavior (agents, other clubs) are common to QO, non-tender and posting, and a forecasting model alone does not solve them.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/62",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 7] The set ignores organizational adoption: a tool matters only if decision owners would change their decisions, which is not tested by a backtest.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/63",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "[Blind spot 8] Terms of use for scraped public data (Statcast, transaction logs, foreign-league sites) were not checked, and public is not necessarily lawful to redistribute.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/64",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "cubs_private_models_and_practices",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/65",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Replace the six with one pre-registered \"dated-snapshot decision audit\" on league-wide winter market decisions (non-tender, QO, posting), scoring forecast calibration against realized prices and outcomes. Cubs-specific tooling would be built only where it beats staff-style baselines out of sample.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/66",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Narrow the arbitration idea to a settle-versus-hearing expected-value calculator that uses exchanged figures and public award history, reported with intervals. Stop if annual hearing counts are too low to bound the error.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/67",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Run the coaching idea as a null-result test: check whether year-T coach ratings predict year-T+1 changes better than a tenure or reputation proxy, with matched controls. Fund it only if intervals are narrow enough to change a hire.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2/claim/68",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212457-b02b8f798c1e/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Defer the postseason roster optimizer, and instead build a reusable matchup simulator only if the series win-probability gain from marginal slots is shown to exceed what noise could hide.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        }
      ],
      "evidence_refs": [
        "objective_context"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "No numeric evidence was supplied (facts is empty), so everything below is critique to be checked, not established fact.",
        "The pooled assumptions attached to the candidates include many that belong to other ideas (rain delays, draft pools, stolen bases). I judged each candidate on its own IDEA text only.",
        "The postseason roster IDEA text (candidates/0/5/idea/1) states only owner, decision and frequency. Value, mechanism and baseline appear only in the unresolved-issues list, so that candidate is under-specified as written.",
        "[Coaching 1] The hire or retain decision recurs yearly, but only a handful of coaching slots turn over per club. Value per decision is plausibly large, yet no supplied evidence sizes it.",
        "[Coaching 2] Public inputs are Statcast, staff announcements and media guides. Assistant and minor-league role titles and dates are likely inconsistent, so the link from coach to player may be mislabeled.",
        "[Coaching 3] The number of coach-movement events with enough players per coach is probably small, and the outcome (player change) is observable but very noisy. Intervals may be too wide to change any hiring decision.",
        "[Coaching 4] Actionability is limited because the Cubs can hire only from available candidates, and coach quality is hard to separate from the hiring club's infrastructure.",
        "[Coaching 5] Sophisticated clubs probably already track player development outcomes by staff internally. Public sources give mostly anecdote and press narrative, not rigorous attribution.",
        "[Coaching 6] It would look useful through regression to the mean, survivorship (coaches get poached after good years), and teams acquiring players they already expect to improve. Pitch-mix changes may be driven by front-office strategy and not by the coach.",
        "[Non-tender 1] The decision recurs every November or December, but the Cubs' marginal cases (borderline tender candidates) are probably few per year. Stake per case is the gap between arbitration salary and replacement cost.",
        "[Non-tender 2] Public arbitration salary projections and the prior-year non-tender lists are public. The set of players other clubs will non-tender is not known when the Cubs decide, so any replacement-pool label built from the final list leaks hindsight unless it is forecast as of a dated snapshot.",
        "[Non-tender 3] Past decisions are many league-wide, and signing price and next-season output are observable. Players signed after non-tender are a selected sample, because injured or declining players are overrepresented.",
        "[Non-tender 4] Actionability is high and cheap to reverse. A club can tender, then trade or release, with partial cost, which weakens the need for a precise model.",
        "[Non-tender 5] Clubs already apply WAR-per-dollar thresholds with internal projections, and public arbitration projections are widely available.",
        "[Non-tender 6] It would look useful through hindsight-labeled replacement pools, and through backtests that count only the non-tendered players who succeeded. A comparison against a strawman threshold also flatters it.",
        "[QO 1] The decision recurs yearly only for players who are QO-eligible, so per-year count may be zero to a few. Stake is a compensation pick versus a one-year salary, and the pick's value depends on CBA terms I could not verify.",
        "[QO 2] Public data on age, WAR, and market depth is available at decision time. Agent intent and private willingness to accept are not public, and they dominate the acceptance outcome.",
        "[QO 3] Public history since the system began is only on the order of a hundred or so offers in total. That is too small for a calibrated model with many features, and each outcome is binary, which makes calibration weak.",
        "[QO 4] The CBA expires around December 2026 (unverified), so QO rules may change right when the model would be used, and backtests may not transfer.",
        "[QO 5] Clubs and public analysts already compare projected market AAV to the QO amount, so the mechanism is largely the baseline stated in the IDEA.",
        "[QO 6] It would look useful by overfitting a few dozen cases and by crediting hindsight on acceptance outcomes that were driven by market shocks.",
        "[Posting 1] Posting events per year are few, and the Cubs bid on a small fraction. Stake per signing is large, but the recurrence is thin.",
        "[Posting 2] Public NPB and KBO stats exist, but pitch-tracking and bat-tracking granularity may not be public or licensed. Whether posting timing and the player's availability are known at decision time varies by year.",
        "[Posting 3] The retrospective sample is small and heterogeneous across pitchers and hitters, ages, and ball and rule eras. MLB outcomes are observable but strongly censored by injury and playing time.",
        "[Posting 4] Actionability depends on posting fees, bid rules, and competition from other clubs. Any accuracy edge must also beat the winner's curse.",
        "[Posting 5] Clubs with international scouting and data feeds already run translation models. Public analysts publish translation factors, so the baseline \"simple ratios\" is probably weaker than actual club practice.",
        "[Posting 6] It would look useful through a handful of memorable hits and misses, and through fitting a model on survivors who were posted because they looked good. Narrow intervals from few cases would be false precision.",
        "[Postseason 1] The decision occurs only when the Cubs qualify, so expected annual value is discounted by playoff probability, and the number of roster slots that matter is small.",
        "[Postseason 2] Opponent and roster information is public only close to the decision time. Injury status at the roster deadline is often incomplete.",
        "[Postseason 3] Public postseason series number only in the dozens each year, and outcomes are dominated by luck. A series win-probability difference of a fraction of a percentage point cannot be detected.",
        "[Postseason 4] Actionable, but constrained by health and by who is actually on the 40-man roster, which leaves few real choices.",
        "[Postseason 5] Contending clubs likely simulate matchups internally and have far better injury information than public sources.",
        "[Postseason 6] It would look useful by scoring simulator-recommended rosters against actual rosters on the same simulator, which only validates the model against itself. Post-hoc stories about a pinch runner are also misleading.",
        "[Arbitration 1] The decision recurs each January for every arbitration-eligible player, so many decisions per year, though hearings are a small subset. The stake is raise levels that compound, and the total is plausibly meaningful but unsized here.",
        "[Arbitration 2] Exchanged figures and hearing results are public. Panel reasoning, comparables admitted and club-specific hearing policy are less visible, and rules may change under a new CBA.",
        "[Arbitration 3] Hearings per year are few, so a panel-outcome predictor trained on public hearings has small n, and the outcome is binary (the panel picks one of two numbers), which carries little information per case.",
        "[Arbitration 4] Actionability is real for the file-and-trial and settlement choice, but a club policy choice (such as whether to go to hearings at all) can matter more than case-by-case prediction.",
        "[Arbitration 5] Clubs and outside counsel have studied hearings for decades, and settlement at midpoint is a well-known baseline. Public databases of arbitration results already exist.",
        "[Arbitration 6] It would look useful by fitting hearing results with too many features, and from selection: hearings are cases the sides could not settle, so they differ from the cases the model would need to price.",
        "[Blind spot 1] No candidate states expected dollars or wins per decision with a source, so ranking by size of stake is currently unsupported.",
        "[Blind spot 2] Every backtest compares against a simple rule, whereas the real competitor is internal staff with private data. Beating the strawman does not show an advantage.",
        "[Blind spot 3] Hindsight risk is shared by all six. Backtests need dated snapshots of what was public at the decision date (projections, rosters, rumors), and many public sources are overwritten.",
        "[Blind spot 4] Small n and multiple testing across features, years and subgroups will produce spurious wins for the QO, posting, postseason, and hearing candidates unless the test is pre-registered.",
        "[Blind spot 5] A CBA expiration around this offseason (unverified) could change arbitration, QO, draft and service rules, and could cause a lockout. Backtests before that date may not carry over.",
        "[Blind spot 6] Winner's curse and counterparty behavior (agents, other clubs) are common to QO, non-tender and posting, and a forecasting model alone does not solve them.",
        "[Blind spot 7] The set ignores organizational adoption: a tool matters only if decision owners would change their decisions, which is not tested by a backtest.",
        "[Blind spot 8] Terms of use for scraped public data (Statcast, transaction logs, foreign-league sites) were not checked, and public is not necessarily lawful to redistribute."
      ],
